        "modifications": [],
        "reasoning": "The isentropic vortex test is a standard test case for evaluating the accuracy of numerical methods in fluid dynamics. In this test, a vortex is advected diagonally in a doubly periodic domain. By running the test on a 64x64 grid and advecting the vortex at (u_inf,v_inf)=(1,1), we can assess the performance of ERF in capturing the vortex's evolution. Computing the L2 density error after one full traversal provides a quantitative measure of the method's accuracy. Baseline weights: configuration_complexity=0.100, development_activity=0.100, domain_models=0.100, grid_specifications=0.200, path_hierarchy=0.150, physics_parameters=0.300, resource_requirements=0.050.",
